
# <prefix>: <what the commit does, in one line>
#
#   feat:     a new feature
#   fix:      a bug fix
#   refactor: a change to the code that keeps its behavior
#   style:    a change to how the app looks
#   chore:    the build, configuration or development setup
#   docs:     documentation only
#
# Examples:
#   feat: add MySQL driver
#   fix: scroll the tab bar when tabs overflow
#
# - Keep the first line within 72 characters, start it in lower case, and end it without a period.
# - Say what the commit does, not which files or functions it touches.
# - When one line is not enough, leave a blank line and list the rest as bullets.
#
#   feat: connect to databases through an SSH tunnel
#
#   - Start the system ssh to forward a local port
#   - Refuse unknown host keys
#
# Lines starting with "#" are left out of the commit message.
